+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Official documentation
======================

See the Teleport documentation at https://goteleport.com/docs/

A quick introduction to Teleport Community Edition is available at:

  https://goteleport.com/docs/get-started/deploy-community/

Keep in mind that the OpenBSD port of ${PKGSTEM} currently lacks the
following features:

- Windows Remote Desktop Protocol

Usage
=====

The following programs are installed by the ${PKGSTEM} package.

Read the official documentation and run the built-in 'help' command of
each tool for further information.

teleport
--------

The main Teleport binary that runs the Web UI, Auth Service, Proxy
Service, and Teleport Agent services.

Some Teleport features require files from the Teleport CDN, which are
distributed under the Teleport Community license:

  https://goteleport.com/blog/teleport-community-license/

To accept this licence and make use of Teleport's CDN, add a login-class
for teleport to login.conf(5) which sets the TELEPORT_CDN_BASE_URL
environment variable to the URL of Teleport's CDN:

teleport:\
        :setenv=TELEPORT_CDN_BASE_URL="https://cdn.teleport.dev":\
        :tc=daemon:

By default, the Teleport server is run with the _teleport user account.
The Teleport server might print a message which claims that it requires
root access because Teleport uses "/var/lib/teleport", which is false.
Another message might suggest to run "sudo teleport start". which is
wrong.  Use "rcctl enable teleport && rcctl start teleport" instead.

Running Teleport as root is only needed in certain use cases, such as
when Teleport will act as an SSH server on the system where Teleport is
running.  To run Teleport as root, set "teleport_user=root" in
/etc/rc.conf.local.

tctl
----

tctl is the administrative command-line interface for managing a
Teleport cluster. It allows administrators to configure roles, manage
users, and work with resources such as tokens, trusted clusters, and
audit logs.

tsh
---

tsh is the command-line tool used by Teleport users to authenticate,
connect to infrastructure resources, and manage active sessions.  It
supports SSH, Kubernetes, databases, and applications.
